he  knockout dancer nancy in 2005  sin city the adaptation of frank  miller's edgy crime comics  suddenly however alba fell off the radar  according to alba herself a big part of  the problem was that she rarely got to  sink her teeth into challenging leading  parts  most of her work was in supporting roles  and many of them featured in poorly  received movies  this equals to both fantastic four and  sin city tanked for example as did most  of her later projects  in a number of interviews over the years  alba has gone back and forth on whether  or not professional acting is a priority  for her anymore  though it's clear she isn't making the  mark on hollywood she once did  she's currently starring in the crime  drama series la's finest the spin-off of  the bad boys films  considering its embarrassing aggregate  score of seven percent on rotten  tomatoes however it doesn't seem like  it's going to be launching alba back  into the a-list anytime soon  before the marvel cinematic universe was  born with 2008's iron man  sam raimi's spider-man movies were  probably the most prolific and  well-loved superhero movies around  and long before andrew garfield or tom  holland even began their careers tomi  maguire had become one of the definitive  superhero movie stars  pizza time while 2002 spider-man and its  2004 follow-up were critical and  commercial hits  2007 spider-man 3 ended the franchise on  a deafening down note  helped by the popularity of the first  two films spider-man 3 at least made  money but both fans and critics were  deeply disappointed  raymie wanted to make spider-man 4 to  redeem himself but that movie never came  to be  spider-man 3 was a serious body blow to  maguire's acting career  he's enjoyed a few leading roles since  but none have reached the prominence or  success of the spider-man flicks  of course maguire has partly  transitioned from starring in films to  producing them  and since spider-man 3 the actor has  spent more time behind the camera than  in front of it  maybe that's just where he's happiest  time will tell if marvel fans are  destined to see an x-force film or  deadpool 3 hit theaters but if these  movies do see the light of day you can  lay some pretty safe bets that tj miller  won't be involved in either  the actor and comedian played wade  wilson's friend weasel in the first two  deadpool films but his acting career  dried up quickly in 2018  miller's trouble started back in 2017  when it was reported he wouldn't be  returning to the hbo series silicon  valley  the show's creative team told vulture  the following year that miller was often  drunk or high on set  and that some days he wouldn't even show  up for work later in 2017  much more serious allegations arose from  a woman claiming miller had sexually  assaulted her in college  finally in march 2018 miller was  arrested for allegedly calling in a fake  bomb threat  deadpool 2 producer lauren schuler  donner said that by the time the sexual  assault allegation surfaced it was too  late to remove miller from the film  but there were signs his role had shrunk  considerably in september 2018  ryan reynolds confirmed that fans  shouldn't expect to see miller in  x-force  miller has since said he's contractually  obligated to appear in deadpool 3 if  disney asks him to be in it but  well don't hold your breath okay so jim  carrey may not be the first actor you  think of when you hear the phrase  superhero movie stars but he's done more  than his fair share of time in the comic  book trenches  in 1994 he starred as an unstable  superhero with shape-shifting powers in  the mask  the following year he played the riddler  in batman forever and in 2013 he  portrayed colonel stars and stripes in  the hyper-violent superhero comedy  kick-ass too  there was a time when a carry comedy was  an automatic moneymaker while some of  his dramas are among the most beloved of  all time  and it's true carrie still makes movies  today but he's not the a-lister he used  to be  these days most of his movie work comes  in the forms of supporting roles in  cameos  there are a few reasons for carrie's  diminished presence in hollywood  for one he's proven fairly difficult to  work with his method acting antics  during the making of man on the moon had  become the stuff of legend  he also refused to help promote kick ass  too because he wasn't comfortable with  the film's violent tone  especially in the aftermath of the sandy  hook killings for another in more recent  years carrie seems perfectly happy to  remain outside the spotlight and on a  number of occasions he stated that he  feels no real urge to make himself any  more famous than he already is  while terence howard played james rhodes  in 2008's iron man it was don cheadle  who donned war machine's armor in  subsequent marvel films howard has since  said that when marvel studios approached  him to renegotiate for iron man 2 they  offered him only 1 8 of what he was  originally promised  howard wasn't shy about expressing his  frustrations toward his friend and  co-star robert downey jr either though  the two would later meant fences  it turns out that the person that i  helped become  iron man took the money that was  supposed to go to me  and pushed me out in the meantime  howard's career didn't seem to suffer  too badly  he even landed the lead role of hip-hop  mogul lucius lyon on the musical drama  empire  despite empire's successful six season  run howard announced in 2019 that he was  going to quit acting for good  so far his reasons for the change have  been unclear mainly because his  responses about the decision in  interviews have been  rather strange for example during an  interview on the red carpet at the 2019  emmy awards howard explained that  i was able to open up the flower of life  and find the real wave conjugations that  we've been looking for for 10  000 years he went on to say that when he  opened the so-called flower of life  i found a whole new world of wave  conjugations that expose the in-between  spaces  it's not particularly clear what howard  means by that but one of the  consequences of the opening of the  flower of life is apparently that he's  going to give up being an actor  can't argue with that kevin spacey  turned out to be one of the more  memorable parts of a fairly forgettable  superhero movie when he replaced gene  hackman as lex luthor in 2006's superman  returns but spacey isn't likely to find  work on a superhero movie or any other  kind of movie anytime soon  that's because spacey has since become  one of the most loaded villains of the  me2 movement  after actor anthony rapp told buzzfeed  news in 2017  that spacey had made unwanted advances  toward him when he was only 14  spacey claimed he had no memory of the  event and apologized for what he called  quote  deeply inappropriate drunken behavior  more allegations followed including  accusations of sexual harassment and  assault from the likes of harry dreyfuss  filmmaker tony montana and crew members  from the spacey-led netflix series house  of cards  as a result of the allegation spacey's  acting career has come to a swift and  decisive end  netflix fired spacey from house of cards  and announced it wouldn't release the  netflix original film gore  in which spacey played the late gore  vidal even though the crime thriller all  the money in the world was already  filmed by that point  spacey was removed from the film and  director ridley scott re-shot all of  spacey scenes with christopher plummer  for all intents and purposes kevin  spacey's hollywood career is dead  and buried aaron eckhart has the  distinction of playing an important  supporting role in one of the best  superhero movies ever made the actor  famously played harvey dent in 2008's  the dark knight  but despite receiving critical acclaim  for that role and a number of others  eckard has never quite taken off as a  leading man in hollywood  he's taken a few shots 